  "notes": "Notion/Linear-style neutral reader: warm-grey sidebar (#f9f9f8-ish) with hairline divider, grey #5f5e5b text throughout, near-black titles. Feeds get colored square letter-favicons (orange Y for HN, purple V for The Verge, etc.) which provide the only color. Segmented tabs use a grey track with a white raised pill for the selected value. Article rows separated by hairline rules, no cards; hover reveals inline row actions (mark read circle, star, open original). Detail opens as a right slide-over with blurred backdrop, toolbar (Mark as read, Star, Original, close) and Previous/Next footer. Command palette (Cmd+K) is a small centered dialog with blurred backdrop. Sidebar and list scroll independently; 'Notifications alt+T' region suggests a toast system (sonner) not visible in capture. Includes Chinese feed folder (中文)."
